{%- comment -%}
  AJ Tee of the Week — one graphic tee, slabbed like a graded collector card.

  A CARD RATHER THAN A DEAL, and the discount arithmetic is the reason. Measured
  on 4 August against the live catalogue: 145 graphic tees, median price $46.00
  against a $27.60 cost, so a 40% margin. Hold a 20% margin floor and a 15% cut
  leaves 93 of the 145 eligible — nearly two years of weekly picks. A 25% cut
  leaves 18, which is four months and then repeats.

  So 15% is the only sustainable number, and 15% is the problem: the Bargain Bin
  two sections up is a permanent 25%, and a shallower discount presented AS a
  discount reads as the worse offer sitting above the better one. A slabbed card
  sidesteps the comparison entirely — it sells scarcity and curation, which is
  what a weekly pick actually is, and lets the 15% arrive as a corner sticker
  rather than the headline. Nothing here claims to beat the Bin.

  THE SLAB, NOT JUST A CARD, and that came out of the graded-card mockup: a
  cream label band carrying the set name and a serial, then the card itself,
  the whole assembly inside a rigid clear case. A bare card is a bordered
  rectangle. A card somebody sealed in plastic is a thing that was judged worth
  protecting, which is the entire argument this section makes. It costs three
  wrapper elements and no image assets.

  NO GRADE NUMBER, and that omission is deliberate rather than an oversight.
  The obvious move is to put a big "9.5" where a graded card carries its grade,
  and it would look terrific — but a grade is a claim about condition, and a
  made-up one on a live storefront is a small lie printed in the largest type on
  the page. The slot holds the week number instead, which is true, sits in the
  same place, and reads the same at a glance.

  THE PERCENTAGE IS COMPUTED, NEVER TYPED. The sticker renders only when the
  variant genuinely carries a compare-at above its price, and prints whatever
  the real gap is. If nobody discounts the product this week the card still
  works — it is a pick, not a sale — and no number appears.

  PICKED BY AN AGENT, ORDERED BY HAND. The product picker wins if it is set;
  otherwise the first product of the tee collection is used, which is what the
  Tee of the Week agent maintains. Clearing the picker hands control back to the
  queue without touching this file.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  # The picker wins, so a manual override never needs a deploy or an agent pause.
  assign tee = s.tee_product
  if tee == blank and s.tee_collection != blank
    assign tee = s.tee_collection.products.first
  endif
-%}

{%- if tee != blank -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign v = tee.selected_or_first_available_variant

    assign off_pct = 0
    if v.compare_at_price > v.price
      assign off_pct = v.compare_at_price | minus: v.price | times: 100 | divided_by: v.compare_at_price
    endif

    # THE SERIES NUMBER IS DERIVED FROM THE CALENDAR, not a field somebody has to
    # remember to bump. A number that silently stops incrementing is worse than
    # no number, because it makes a weekly section look abandoned. 604800 is a
    # week in seconds.
    assign anchor_s = s.series_start | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign now_s = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
    assign week_no = now_s | minus: anchor_s | divided_by: 604800 | plus: 1
    if week_no < 1
      assign week_no = 1
    endif

    # Zero-padded to three digits, applied cumulatively — testing `week_no`
    # against both bounds while re-deriving from the raw number each time would
    # give single digits only one zero.
    assign week_label = week_no | append: ''
    if week_no < 100
      assign week_label = week_label | prepend: '0'
    endif
    if week_no < 10
      assign week_label = week_label | prepend: '0'
    endif

    # Size range off whichever option is actually named size. Suppliers in this
    # catalogue are not consistent about option ORDER, so matching on the name is
    # the only reliable read.
    assign size_first = ''
    assign size_last = ''
    for opt in tee.options_with_values
      assign opt_name = opt.name | downcase
      if opt_name contains 'size'
        assign size_first = opt.values | first
        assign size_last = opt.values | last
      endif
    endfor

    # The slab serial. A real one, not a random string: the variant's SKU if the
    # supplier set one, otherwise the product id, which is stable and unique.
    assign serial = v.sku
    if serial == blank
      assign serial = tee.id
    endif
  -%}

  <div
    class="aj-teew color-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
    style="padding-block-start: {{ s.padding-block-start }}px; padding-block-end: {{ s.padding-block-end }}px;"
    {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    <div class="aj-teew__inner page-width">
      {%- comment -%}
        The slab leads on desktop and the copy sits beside it, because the slab
        IS the argument — a paragraph explaining that a t-shirt is collectible
        persuades nobody, and a sealed numbered card does it without a sentence.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="aj-teew__stage">
        <div class="aj-teew__slab" data-aj-tilt>
          {%- comment -%}
            The case itself: one element for the plastic, one for the light
            running across it. Both inert.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="aj-teew__glass" aria-hidden="true"></span>

          {%- comment -%}
            The grading label. Set name on the left, week number where a grade
            would sit, serial and barcode beneath — the barcode is drawn with a
            repeating gradient, so it encodes nothing and claims nothing.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="aj-teew__label">
            <div class="aj-teew__label-l">
              <span class="aj-teew__label-set">{{ s.card_series | escape }}</span>
              <span class="aj-teew__label-sub">{{ s.card_subset | escape }}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="aj-teew__label-r">
              <span class="aj-teew__label-wk">Wk</span>
              <span class="aj-teew__label-no">{{ week_label }}</span>
            </div>
            <span class="aj-teew__barcode" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="aj-teew__serial">{{ serial | escape }}</span>
          </div>

          <article class="aj-teew__card">
            <span class="aj-teew__bands" aria-hidden="true"></span>

            <div class="aj-teew__cardin">
              <span class="aj-teew__roundel" aria-hidden="true">Y</span>

              <a
                class="aj-teew__window aj-teew__window--{{ s.window_style }}"
                href="{{ tee.url }}"
                tabindex="-1"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                {%- liquid
                  assign art = s.tee_image
                  if art == blank
                    assign art = tee.featured_image
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- if art != blank -%}
                  {{
                    art
                    | image_url: width: 900
                    | image_tag:
                      loading: 'lazy',
                      widths: '360, 540, 720, 900',
                      sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 32vw, 72vw',
                      class: 'aj-teew__art',
                      alt: ''
                  }}
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>

              {%- comment -%}
                The name plate, which on a real card is the only place the
                subject is named — so the product title goes here and nowhere
                else on the slab.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <div class="aj-teew__plate">
                <h3 class="aj-teew__name">{{ tee.title | escape }}</h3>
                <p class="aj-teew__plate-sub">
                  <span aria-hidden="true">&#9733;</span>
                  {{ s.card_subset | escape }}
                  <span aria-hidden="true">&#9733;</span>
                </p>
              </div>

              {%- comment -%}
                Every figure here is read off the product. Nothing in this strip
                is typed into the editor, so it cannot drift away from the thing
                it describes.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <dl class="aj-teew__strip">
                <div class="aj-teew__stat">
                  <dt>Price</dt>
                  <dd class="aj-teew__stat-price">{{ v.price | money }}</dd>
                </div>
                {%- if off_pct > 0 -%}
                  <div class="aj-teew__stat">
                    <dt>Was</dt>
                    <dd><s>{{ v.compare_at_price | money }}</s></dd>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if size_first != blank -%}
                  <div class="aj-teew__stat">
                    <dt>Sizes</dt>
                    <dd>
                      {{- size_first | escape -}}
                      {%- if size_last != size_first %}&ndash;{{ size_last | escape }}{% endif -%}
                    </dd>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </dl>

              <span class="aj-teew__sheen" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </div>
          </article>

          {%- if off_pct > 0 -%}
            <span class="aj-teew__flag">{{ off_pct }}% off</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="aj-teew__copy">
        {%- if s.kicker != blank -%}
          <p class="aj-teew__kicker">{{ s.kicker | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.heading != blank -%}
          <h2 class="aj-teew__heading">{{ s.heading | escape }}</h2>
          {%- comment -%}
            The same four colours in the same order as the card's own band. Two
            halves of a section sitting on a flat ground read as two things; one
            repeated element makes them one.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="aj-teew__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.body != blank -%}
          <p class="aj-teew__body">{{ s.body | escape }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- comment -%}
          A sold-out pick is a real possibility on a section that holds one
          product for seven days, and a live buy button on a dead product is
          worse than an honest label.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          TWO ACTIONS, ONE OF THEM ALWAYS AVAILABLE. Buying is the primary and
          it disappears when the tee sells out — but "see the rest of the set"
          is the more interesting click for anyone who came for the collecting
          rather than the shirt, and it is the ONLY thing left to offer when
          the week's card is gone. So the archive link sits outside the
          availability branch and renders either way.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="aj-teew__actions">
          {%- if tee.available -%}
            <a class="aj-teew__cta" href="{{ tee.url }}">
              {{- s.cta_label | escape -}}
              <span aria-hidden="true">&nbsp;&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          {%- else -%}
            <p class="aj-teew__gone">{{ s.sold_out_label | escape }}</p>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if s.archive_label != blank and s.archive_link != blank -%}
            <a class="aj-teew__cta2" href="{{ s.archive_link }}">
              {{- s.archive_label | escape -}}
            </a>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    PROGRESSIVE ENHANCEMENT, NOT A DEPENDENCY. Everything above already works —
    the slab lifts, straightens and catches the light on hover in pure CSS. This
    adds cursor tracking, which is the difference between a card that reacts and
    a card that feels held. If it never runs, nothing is missing.

    It writes rotation into two custom properties rather than setting `transform`
    directly, so the CSS keeps ownership of how they are composed.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.querySelector('#shopify-section-{{ section.id }}');
      if (!root) return;
      if (!window.matchMedia('(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)').matches) return;
      if (window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches) return;

      var slab = root.querySelector('[data-aj-tilt]');
      var stage = root.querySelector('.aj-teew__stage');
      if (!slab || !stage) return;

      var MAX = 9; // degrees; past ~12 the case reads as a glitch rather than a tilt
      var frame = null;

      function track(event) {
        if (frame) return;
        frame = requestAnimationFrame(function () {
          frame = null;
          var box = slab.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (!box.width || !box.height) return;
          var px = (event.clientX - box.left) / box.width - 0.5;
          var py = (event.clientY - box.top) / box.height - 0.5;
          slab.style.setProperty('--aj-teew-ry', (px * MAX * 2).toFixed(2) + 'deg');
          slab.style.setProperty('--aj-teew-rx', (py * -MAX * 2).toFixed(2) + 'deg');
        });
      }

      function release() {
        if (frame) {
          cancelAnimationFrame(frame);
          frame = null;
        }
        slab.style.setProperty('--aj-teew-ry', '0deg');
        slab.style.setProperty('--aj-teew-rx', '0deg');
      }

      stage.addEventListener('pointermove', track);
      stage.addEventListener('pointerleave', release);
    })();
  </script>
{%- endif -%}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
    A PURPLE BAND, and the choice was made by what the homepage had already
    spent. `aj-how` runs cyan and `aj-story` runs yellow, so a third section in
    either turns the page into stripes of the same two colours. Purple is the
    remaining brand colour with enough contrast to hold white type, and it is
    the one that reads as a display case rather than a banner, which is the
    whole idea here. A cream slab on purple is also the highest-contrast
    pairing available — the card has to be the first thing seen.
  */
  .aj-teew {
    --aj-teew-cream: #f2ead9;
    --aj-teew-cream-2: #e4d8c0;
    background: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
    color: #ffffff;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .aj-teew__inner {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    justify-items: center;
    max-width: 64rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teew__inner {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: center;
      gap: 3.5rem;
      justify-items: stretch;
    }
  }

  /* ---- the slab ---------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    The perspective lives on the stage rather than the slab, because an element
    that owns its own perspective rotates around its own centre and reads flat.
    On the parent, the vanishing point stays put and the slab turns inside it.
  */
  .aj-teew__stage {
    perspective: 1400px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 22rem;
    justify-self: center;
  }

  /*
    THE RIGID CASE. Translucent white over the purple ground with a bright inner
    top edge and a dark bottom one — two inset shadows are what make a flat
    panel read as a moulded bevel, and they cost nothing.

    It rests at a slight lean and straightens when you reach for it, which is
    the whole gesture the mockup's leaning card was doing.
  */
  .aj-teew__slab {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.55rem 0.55rem 0.7rem;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, rgb(255 255 255 / 0.34), rgb(255 255 255 / 0.12));
    border: 1px solid rgb(255 255 255 / 0.5);
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.7),
      inset 0 -1px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.18),
      0 22px 44px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.42);

    /*
      TWO TRANSFORM SYSTEMS, DELIBERATELY SEPARATED — the same rule aj-how
      documents. The pointer tilt owns `transform`; the resting lean owns
      `rotate` and the hover lift owns `translate` and `scale`, which are
      independent properties applied before it. Written as one `transform`, a
      pointermove would overwrite the lift on its next frame and the slab would
      drop mid-hover.
    */
    transform: rotateX(var(--aj-teew-rx, 0deg)) rotateY(var(--aj-teew-ry, 0deg));
    rotate: -2.5deg;
    transition: translate 0.25s ease, scale 0.25s ease, rotate 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease;
    will-change: transform;
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-teew__stage:hover .aj-teew__slab {
      translate: 0 -8px;
      scale: 1.02;
      rotate: 0deg;
      box-shadow:
        inset 0 1px 0 rgb(255 255 255 / 0.8),
        inset 0 -1px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2),
        0 32px 60px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
    }
  }

  /* The one highlight that says "there is plastic in front of this". */
  .aj-teew__glass {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 3;
    pointer-events: none;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      118deg,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 34%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.16) 44%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.04) 52%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 62%
    );
  }

  /* ---- the grading label -------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teew__label {
    position: relative;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    align-items: start;
    gap: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem 0.45rem;
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--aj-teew-cream, #f2ead9);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    /* The label is a separate printed insert, so it gets its own edge. */
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25), inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  }

  .aj-teew__label-l {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .aj-teew__label-set {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .aj-teew__label-sub {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.1;
    opacity: 0.62;
  }

  /*
    Where a graded card carries its grade. It carries the week instead — see the
    note at the top of this file. Set at the same weight a grade would be,
    because the slot's job is to be the loudest number on the label.
  */
  .aj-teew__label-r {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    justify-self: end;
  }

  .aj-teew__label-wk {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }

  .aj-teew__label-no {
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 0.85;
  }

  /*
    Drawn, not encoded. Irregular bar widths from a repeating gradient with four
    stops — an even comb reads as a texture, uneven bars read as a barcode.
  */
  .aj-teew__barcode {
    grid-column: 1;
    height: 0.85rem;
    align-self: end;
    background-image: repeating-linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828) 0 1px,
      transparent 1px 3px,
      var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828) 3px 5px,
      transparent 5px 6px,
      var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828) 6px 7px,
      transparent 7px 10px
    );
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .aj-teew__serial {
    grid-column: 2;
    align-self: end;
    justify-self: end;
    max-width: 9rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  /* ---- the card ---------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    Cream stock with everything printed on it in brand colour, which is how a
    real card works: the paper is neutral and the team owns the ink. A card in
    brand purple on a brand purple band would simply disappear.
  */
  .aj-teew__card {
    position: relative;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.4rem;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--aj-teew-cream, #f2ead9), var(--aj-teew-cream-2, #e4d8c0));
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.16);
  }

  /* Team colours, four hard stops. The one element that is purely brand. */
  .aj-teew__bands {
    display: block;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8) 0 25%,
      var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000) 25% 50%,
      var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0) 50% 75%,
      var(--aj-brand-teal, #30aac6) 75% 100%
    );
  }

  .aj-teew__cardin {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-block-start: 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 5px;
  }

  /*
    The roundel a card puts its league mark in. A Flashy "Y" rather than a star,
    because a star belongs to every card ever printed and the Y belongs to this
    shop.
  */
  .aj-teew__roundel {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0.4rem;
    left: 0.4rem;
    z-index: 2;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1;
    /* Flashy's caps sit high in the em box, so centring on the box leaves the
       glyph visibly above the circle's middle. Nudged down by eye. */
    padding-block-start: 0.14em;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828), 0 2px 5px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.3);
  }

  /*
    THREE WINDOW MODES, BECAUSE THE CATALOGUE IS NOT ONE THING. Checked against
    live product images on 4 August: Parallel, who supply 87 of the 145 eligible
    tees, shoot flat-lay on CONCRETE. Obsessed With Graphic Tees shoot on white.
    A single treatment flatters one and ruins the other.

    Photo is the default and it is the one the graded-card reference actually
    uses — that mockup's window holds a full-bleed action shot, not a cut-out.
    A concrete-backed tee cropped to fill reads exactly like card photography,
    so the supplier's least convenient habit turns out to be the right asset.

    Cut-out is for later: a background-free PNG floating on a halftone field.
    White is the honest fallback for stock already shot on white, where cover
    would crop the tee and contain would at least sit on matching ground.
  */
  .aj-teew__window {
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
  }

  .aj-teew__window--cutout {
    background-color: var(--aj-brand-teal, #30aac6);
    background-image: radial-gradient(rgb(255 255 255 / 0.3) 1.5px, transparent 1.6px);
    background-size: 9px 9px;
  }

  .aj-teew__window--white {
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .aj-teew__art {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
  }

  /*
    Cover for the photo mode, so the shot fills the frame the way card
    photography does. Contain everywhere else, so a cut-out is never cropped.
  */
  .aj-teew__window--photo .aj-teew__art {
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .aj-teew__window--cutout .aj-teew__art,
  .aj-teew__window--white .aj-teew__art {
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* Lifts a cut-out off the field so it reads as an object on the card. */
  .aj-teew__window--cutout .aj-teew__art {
    filter: drop-shadow(0 6px 10px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28));
  }

  /* ---- the name plate ----------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teew__plate {
    padding: 0.6rem 0.7rem 0.5rem;
    text-align: center;
    background: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    color: var(--aj-teew-cream, #f2ead9);
  }

  .aj-teew__name {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 4.2vw, 1.45rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .aj-teew__plate-sub {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  /* ---- the stat strip ----------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teew__strip {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.55rem;
    background: var(--aj-teew-cream, #f2ead9);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.5625rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border-block-start: 2px solid rgb(0 0 0 / 0.14);
  }

  .aj-teew__stat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.12rem;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .aj-teew__stat + .aj-teew__stat {
    padding-inline-start: 0.5rem;
    border-inline-start: 1px dotted rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22);
  }

  .aj-teew__stat dt {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  .aj-teew__stat dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-overflow: ellipsis;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .aj-teew__stat-price {
    color: var(--aj-brand-purple, #7a3fa0);
  }

  .aj-teew__stat s {
    opacity: 0.55;
  }

  /* ---- the sticker -------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    Cocked at an angle on the corner of the case, like something applied after
    sealing. Small on purpose: the week number is the headline, not this.
  */
  .aj-teew__flag {
    position: absolute;
    top: -0.55rem;
    right: -0.6rem;
    z-index: 4;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    rotate: 7deg;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.32);
  }

  /* ---- the sheen ---------------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    Clipped by the card's inner box, never interactive, and it owns `translate`
    alone so it cannot collide with the slab's tilt.
  */
  .aj-teew__sheen {
    position: absolute;
    inset-block: -30%;
    inset-inline-start: 0;
    z-index: 2;
    width: 55%;
    pointer-events: none;
    translate: -190% 0;
    rotate: 8deg;
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 0%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.2) 40%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.55) 50%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0.2) 60%,
      rgb(255 255 255 / 0) 100%
    );
  }

  @media (hover: hover) {
    .aj-teew__sheen {
      transition: translate 0.8s cubic-bezier(0.22, 0.61, 0.36, 1);
    }

    .aj-teew__stage:hover .aj-teew__sheen {
      translate: 320% 0;
    }
  }

  /* ---- the copy column ---------------------------------------------------- */

  .aj-teew__copy {
    text-align: center;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teew__copy {
      text-align: start;
    }
  }

  .aj-teew__kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-teew__rule {
    display: block;
    width: 8rem;
    height: 5px;
    margin: 0 auto 1rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    /*
      INK WHERE THE CARD USES PURPLE. The card's band sits on cream, where all
      four brand colours read. This one sits on the purple ground, and rendered
      with the card's exact palette the third segment simply vanished — a
      four-colour bar with a hole in it. Ink is the substitution that keeps the
      rhythm without inventing a fifth brand colour.
    */
    background: linear-gradient(
      90deg,
      var(--aj-brand-cyan, #5cd8f8) 0 25%,
      var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000) 25% 50%,
      var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828) 50% 75%,
      var(--aj-brand-teal, #30aac6) 75% 100%
    );
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teew__rule {
      margin-inline: 0;
    }
  }

  .aj-teew__heading {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    font-family: "Flashy", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6.5vw, 3.25rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .aj-teew__body {
    margin: 0 auto 1.4rem;
    max-width: 36ch;
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.86);
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teew__body {
      margin-inline: 0;
    }
  }

  .aj-teew__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 0.75rem 1rem;
  }

  @media screen and (min-width: 750px) {
    .aj-teew__actions {
      justify-content: flex-start;
    }
  }

  .aj-teew__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    color: var(--aj-brand-ink, #282828);
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: translate 0.15s ease, box-shadow 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-teew__cta:hover {
    translate: 0 -2px;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28);
  }

  /*
    A LINK, NOT A SECOND BUTTON. Two filled buttons side by side make a reader
    choose before they know what either does, and this one is the lesser of the
    two on a section whose job is to sell the tee in front of them. Underlined
    rather than outlined so it reads as somewhere to go rather than something
    to press.
  */
  .aj-teew__cta2 {
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #ffffff;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
    text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    transition: color 0.15s ease;
  }

  .aj-teew__cta2:hover {
    color: var(--aj-brand-yellow, #ffe000);
  }

  .aj-teew__gone {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: "Ohpixel", var(--font-heading--family);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 0.66);
  }

  /* ---- motion on touch ---------------------------------------------------- */

  /*
    A PHONE HAS NO HOVER, so the two effects that carry this section on desktop
    are unreachable there. Scroll position substitutes for the pointer: the card
    rises into place and the sheen sweeps once as it arrives. Same approach and
    the same two guards as aj-how — @supports for browsers with no view
    timeline, which simply see the finished state, and reduced-motion for people
    who asked not to have any of it.

    THE RISE IS ON THE CARD AND THE LIFT IS ON THE SLAB, which is not tidiness.
    An animation with `both` holds its end state and wins over a plain
    declaration, so a hover rule setting `translate` on the same element the
    entrance animates would simply never apply. Different elements, no contest.
  */
  @supports (animation-timeline: view()) {
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      .aj-teew__card {
        animation: aj-teew-rise linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 5% cover 32%;
      }

      @keyframes aj-teew-rise {
        from {
          opacity: 0;
          translate: 0 26px;
        }

        to {
          opacity: 1;
          translate: 0 0;
        }
      }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) and (hover: none) {
      .aj-teew__sheen {
        animation: aj-teew-sweep linear both;
        animation-timeline: view();
        animation-range: entry 40% cover 55%;
      }

      @keyframes aj-teew-sweep {
        from {
          translate: -190% 0;
        }

        to {
          translate: 320% 0;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .aj-teew__inner {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 1.6rem;
    }

    /*
      The copy leads on a phone. Stacked in source order the slab would come
      first and push the heading below the fold, so the reader meets an
      unlabelled object. On desktop both are visible at once and the slab leads.
    */
    .aj-teew__copy {
      order: -1;
    }

    .aj-teew__stage {
      max-width: 19rem;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "AJ Tee of the Week",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "One graphic tee a week, presented as a graded collector card. The week number increments from the series start date on its own — nothing to bump."
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "This week's tee" },
    { "type": "product", "id": "tee_product", "label": "Tee" },
    {
      "type": "collection",
      "id": "tee_collection",
      "label": "Fallback collection",
      "info": "Used only when no tee is picked above — takes the first product. This is what the Tee of the Week agent maintains."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "tee_image",
      "label": "Cut-out image",
      "info": "Optional. A background-free PNG of the tee, square, centred, with a little padding. Overrides the product's own image on this card only."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "window_style",
      "label": "Card window",
      "info": "Photo fills the frame — right for tees shot on concrete, which is most of them. Cut-out floats a background-free PNG on a halftone field. White suits stock shot on white.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "photo", "label": "Photo (fills the frame)" },
        { "value": "cutout", "label": "Cut-out on halftone" },
        { "value": "white", "label": "Plain white" }
      ],
      "default": "photo"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Copy" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "One a week" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Tee of the Week" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "One graphic tee, pulled from the pile and sealed up for seven days. Then it goes back and a new one takes its place."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Button", "default": "Yoink it" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "archive_label",
      "label": "Archive link text",
      "info": "Shows whether or not this week's tee is in stock — when it sells out this is the only thing left to click.",
      "default": "See the whole set"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "archive_link",
      "label": "Archive link",
      "info": "The agent creates /collections/tee-past on its first rotation."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "sold_out_label", "label": "Sold-out text", "default": "Gone — back next week with a new one" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Card" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "card_series", "label": "Label set name", "default": "The Yoink" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "card_subset", "label": "Label subset", "default": "Tee of the Week" },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "series_start",
      "label": "Series start date",
      "info": "YYYY-MM-DD. Week 1 begins here; the number climbs by one every seven days.",
      "default": "2026-08-04"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "color_scheme", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Color scheme", "default": "scheme-1" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Padding" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-start", "label": "Top", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 56 },
    { "type": "range", "id": "padding-block-end", "label": "Bottom", "min": 0, "max": 100, "step": 4, "unit": "px", "default": 56 }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "AJ Tee of the Week" }]
}
